course: dictionary
lesson: 1033
title: Boost: lift, help, or sell?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «boost» can mean three things, so look at the words around it. In «a good breakfast boosts energy», boosts means makes energy bigger or better, because the food is what raises your energy.
explain: Boost can also be a noun, meaning help or encouragement. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. «Praise gives her a boost» makes sense if you put in "a lift of encouragement", so a boost is help that makes something rise.
explain: Watch out for boost used to sell things. «Adverts love words like «boost your immune system»», but that is a selling word, not science. Ask yourself: is the advert trying to sell me something, or is it giving me a clear fact?
fact: To boost something means to make it bigger, stronger or better.
fact: A boost is help or encouragement that makes something rise or improve.
fact: «A booster seat» lifts a child up in a car, so the seat belt fits them safely.
fact: «Boost» is a selling word too: adverts use it, but it is not always science.
fact: «No single food or drink can boost the immune system»; sleep, a good diet and exercise keep it working well.
exercise: «A good breakfast boosts energy.» What does boosts mean here? | *Makes energy bigger or better | Makes breakfast smaller | Makes energy disappear
exercise: Mia said no when her friend offered to boost her rank. Why? | It was too late in the day | *It would not be her own rank, and she would have to share her password | She already had diamond rank
exercise: What does a booster seat do for a child in a car? | Keeps the child asleep | Makes the car go faster | *Lifts the child up so the seat belt fits safely
test: What does the replay show about Finn's «speed boost from nowhere»? | *It was a crash into a wall, not real help | It made him win the race | It was a real power-up from a friend
test: Which meaning of boost fits «rockets have booster engines»? | Makes the rocket smaller | Stops the rocket from moving | *Adds an extra push to help it rise | Is a fuel tank for cooking
exam: What is a sensible question to ask about an advert that says «boost your immune system»? | Who is the advert's favourite actor? | *Is this a true science fact, or a word chosen to sell? | Can I buy it at the shop right now? | Will it taste nice?
